Local review patch: propagate T6032 CPU-start rejection to callers
Base: m1n1 4184923ffb2dff079b384d6a32cc02142aa14572, after 0001..0006
Provenance: AI-assisted Debian project work; not submitted upstream.

Return a negative status for rejected T6032 startup. Zero means the caller
may continue under the existing policy, not that every legacy CPU started.
Preserve best-effort behavior for other SoCs. Record pre-release leaf failure
without changing allocation ownership or fatal post-release timeout policy.

Payload and HV callers stop their remaining work on rejection. Existing
cpufreq and PCIe/display/USB preludes retain their ordering and are not
rolled back. Proxy SMP/HV-init commands return S_BADSTATE, which existing
clients already reject as a nonzero status. This is not a global proxy
command sandbox and does not enable T6032 startup dispatch.

